# get_up — success
#
# GET UP exists only in the get-up phase, which follows the childhood reminescences — so like
# cli/remember/, this test must NOT pass --skip-childhood, the flag every other script in the suite
# uses. That is why the verb had no test.
#
# Reaching it means playing the whole childhood out: four reminescences, each a full
# observe -> think -> act chain plus a footer CONTINUE to move to the next. The loop below is those
# four, unrolled — the count is fixed by --seed 42 — a script has no repetition, and unrolling reads better than pretending otherwise.
#
# The phase itself skips the critic and forces difficulty 1 (NarrativeController's GET-UP
# short-circuit), so failure loops back with no penalty rather than producing a FAILURE outcome —
# there is no meaningful fail.cli, and cli/get_up/ has one script deliberately.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode ChildhoodReminescence 60

# ── The three childhood reminescences ────────────────────────────────────────
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 20 180
click button
advance 12 180

advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 20 180
click button
advance 12 180

advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 20 180
click button
advance 12 180

advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 20 180
click button
advance 12 180

# ── The get-up phase ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
wait mode GetUp 60
advance 12 180
regions

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 20 180

# What makes this a get_up test rather than an any-verb test.
expect-verb get_up
quit
